{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nVanya has a scales for weighing loads and weights of masses w0,\u2009w1,\u2009w2,\u2009...,\u2009w100 grams where w is some integer not less than 2 (exactly one weight of each nominal value). Vanya wonders whether he can weight an item with mass m using the given weights, if the weights can be put on both pans of the scales. Formally speaking, your task is to determine whether it is possible to place an item of mass m and some weights on the left pan of the scales, and some weights on the right pan of the scales so that the pans of the scales were in balance.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().run();\n    }\n\n    private void run() {\n        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n             PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out)) {\n            String[] line = br.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            long w = Long.parseLong(line[0]);\n            long m = Long.parseLong(line[1]);\n\n            if (m == 1) {\n                pw.println(\"YES\");\n                return;\n            }\n\n            Set<Long> reachable = new HashSet<>();\n            reachable.add(1L);\n            long currentWeight = w;\n\n            for (int step = 1; step <= 60; step++) {\n                Set<Long> nextReachable = new HashSet<>(reachable);\n                for (Long val : reachable) {\n                    nextReachable.add(val + currentWeight);\n                    nextReachable.add(Math.abs(val - currentWeight));\n                }\n                reachable = nextReachable;\n                if (reachable.contains(m)) {\n                    pw.println(\"YES\");\n                    return;\n                }\n                if (currentWeight > m * w) break;\n                currentWeight *= w;\n            }\n\n            pw.println(\"NO\");\n        } catch (IOException e) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(e);\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().run();\n    }\n\n    private void run() {\n        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n             PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out)) {\n            String[] line = br.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            long w = Long.parseLong(line[0]);\n            long m = Long.parseLong(line[1]);\n\n            // We can place weights on both pans, so for each weight w^i, we can:\n            // - Put it on the same side as the item (adds to left side)\n            // - Put it on the opposite side (subtracts from left side)\n            // - Not use it at all\n            // This means we need to check if m can be represented as a sum of terms \n            // of the form \u00b1w^i (where i ranges from 0 to 100)\n\n            // The key insight: at each step, m should be representable in balanced \n            // base-w notation using digits -1, 0, 1.\n\n            boolean possible = true;\n            for (int i = 0; i <= 100; i++) {\n                long remainder = m % w;\n                \n                // remainder should be 0, 1, or w-1 (which represents -1 in balanced notation)\n                if (remainder == 0) {\n                    // no weight needed at this position\n                    m /= w;\n                } else if (remainder == 1) {\n                    // use one weight on the opposite pan\n                    m = (m - 1) / w;\n                } else if (remainder == w - 1) {\n                    // use one weight on the same pan as the item (equivalent to -1)\n                    m = (m + 1) / w;\n                } else {\n                    possible = false;\n                    break;\n                }\n                \n                if (m == 0) break;\n            }\n\n            pw.println(possible ? \"YES\" : \"NO\");\n        } catch (IOException e) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(e);\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0006129055400379002, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -2.992108420585282e-05, -2.2053474822314456e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -8.583032467868179e-06, -5.722029527532868e-06, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.2543604902457446e-05, -6.437280717364047e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.814689989667386e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.749579137656838e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, -2.95634672511369e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -5.6265202147187665e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.015949550899677e-05, -4.17231